1322:
(a) Every person desiring to engage in the business of operating taxicabs in the city shall, in each and every year in which the business is proposed to be carried on, first make a written application per City of St. Marys Code of Ordinances for an occupational license.
(b) Applications shall be in writing, notarized and filed with the planning department.
(c) The application shall contain:
(1) The full name and address of the applicant and the location from which the proposed business is to be operated;
(2) If a corporation, the name of all the officers or if a partnership, the name of all the partners;
(3) The number of vehicles to be operated under such license, if granted;
(4) The type of automobiles to be used together with the VIN and tag number of each vehicle;
(5) A copy of the minimum liability insurance coverage;
(6) A copy of the each operator's valid driver's license.
(Ord. of 6-9-08(3), §§ 1, 2)

1327:
(a) The city marshal may suspend or revoke any occupational license issued pursuant to the terms of this chapter where the city marshal finds and determines, after notice to the permit holder and an opportunity to be heard that:
(1) One or more illegal sales and/or transportation of controlled substances have occurred in the licensed vehicle or such vehicle has been utilized for the purpose of or in connection with one or more such sales and/or transportation;
(2) Persons have been permitted to utilize such vehicle who are known to the owner or operator, or in the exercise of ordinary care should be known to the owner or operator, or who are reputed to be, illegal sellers or purveyors of controlled substances;
(3) If the holder thereof violates any of the provisions of this chapter or is convicted in any court of violating any law relating to alcoholic beverages or controlled substances or has been convicted of driving a taxicab or other motor vehicle while under the influence of alcoholic beverages or drugs or is convicted of violating the traffic laws or ordinances of the city or defect or impairment of vision. It shall be mandatory that such owner's occupational license be revoked if the owner is convicted for driving while under the influence of alcohol or drugs.
(b) From the decision of the city marshal in revoking any such occupational license, the person holding such occupational license shall have the right to file an appeal. Any person whose occupational license is suspended or revoked by the city marshal may file an appeal to the St. Marys City Manager within 20 days of the denial. The city manager shall have the authority, upon the hearing of the appeal to reverse, vacate or modify the occupational license revocation. The city manger's denial may be appealed to the city council by submitting a written appeal request to city council within 20 days of the denial. The city council shall have the authority, upon the hearing of the appeal to reverse, vacate or modify the occupational license revocation.
(Ord. of 6-9-08(3), §§ 1, 2)

